1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,437
A coconut falls from a
tall tree and lands hard.

2
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:05,938
A hammer, lifted high, drives a nail.

3
00:00:06,338 --> 00:00:07,873
Nobody pushed them down.

4
00:00:07,873 --> 00:00:10,072
So where did that energy come from?

5
00:00:10,522 --> 00:00:12,747
Diya opens the tap on the ground floor.

6
00:00:12,747 --> 00:00:14,806
The water tank sits up on the roof.

7
00:00:15,156 --> 00:00:18,468
Nobody is pushing the water,
yet it gushes out fast.

8
00:00:18,468 --> 00:00:20,240
What is the water carrying?

9
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:24,345
By the end of this video, you
will measure it in joules.

10
00:00:24,995 --> 00:00:27,765
So what is gravitational potential energy?

11
00:00:28,115 --> 00:00:30,302
Lift a book onto a high shelf.

12
00:00:30,302 --> 00:00:32,629
Your arms do work against gravity.

13
00:00:33,029 --> 00:00:34,512
That work is not lost.

14
00:00:34,512 --> 00:00:37,525
It is stored in the book,
because of its height.

15
00:00:37,925 --> 00:00:42,057
Let it fall, and gravity gives
the energy back, as motion.

16
00:00:42,457 --> 00:00:47,344
Energy stored because of height is
called gravitational potential energy,

17
00:00:47,344 --> 00:00:48,244
U.

18
00:00:48,449 --> 00:00:49,416
Let's run it.

19
00:00:49,416 --> 00:00:52,362
A two kilogram ball,
lifted slowly by a rope.

20
00:00:52,712 --> 00:00:56,963
To lift it slowly, the rope pulls
up with nineteen point six newtons.

21
00:00:56,963 --> 00:00:59,024
That is just its weight, m g.

22
00:00:59,424 --> 00:01:03,432
One metre up, the rope has done
nineteen point six joules of work.

23
00:01:03,832 --> 00:01:07,290
Every metre adds the same
nineteen point six joules.

24
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:10,228
At five metres, U is ninety eight joules.

25
00:01:10,628 --> 00:01:13,481
On the graph, U against
height is a straight line.

26
00:01:13,481 --> 00:01:15,598
Double the height, double the energy.

27
00:01:16,098 --> 00:01:17,272
Now let it go.

28
00:01:17,272 --> 00:01:19,603
The stored energy turns into speed.

29
00:01:20,003 --> 00:01:22,178
Slow-mo replay, halfway down.

30
00:01:22,528 --> 00:01:26,222
The weight still points down,
and the speed keeps growing.

31
00:01:26,222 --> 00:01:28,583
Gravity hands back the stored energy.

32
00:01:29,233 --> 00:01:31,419
Now the formula, step by step.

33
00:01:31,769 --> 00:01:32,669
Step one.

34
00:01:32,669 --> 00:01:37,647
To lift it slowly, the upward
force F must equal the weight, m g.

35
00:01:38,397 --> 00:01:39,297
Step two.

36
00:01:39,231 --> 00:01:41,528
Force and movement both point up.

37
00:01:41,528 --> 00:01:43,936
So the work is force times height.

38
00:01:43,936 --> 00:01:45,257
W equals m g h.

39
00:01:46,007 --> 00:01:46,934
Step three.

40
00:01:46,934 --> 00:01:48,436
That work is stored.

41
00:01:48,436 --> 00:01:51,509
U equals m g h, taking the ground as zero.

42
00:01:52,259 --> 00:01:53,159
Step four.

43
00:01:53,098 --> 00:01:53,998
Units.

44
00:01:53,687 --> 00:01:57,332
Kilograms, times metres per
second squared, times metres.

45
00:01:57,332 --> 00:01:58,232
Joules.

46
00:01:58,719 --> 00:01:59,669
Step five.

47
00:01:59,669 --> 00:02:03,057
Going up, gravity does
minus m g h of work.

48
00:02:03,057 --> 00:02:05,701
U is the work done against gravity.

49
00:02:06,451 --> 00:02:07,547
Remember this.

50
00:02:07,547 --> 00:02:12,372
U equals m g h, where h is the
height above the level you call zero.

51
00:02:13,072 --> 00:02:14,542
But height above what?

52
00:02:14,542 --> 00:02:15,725
Follow the links.

53
00:02:16,075 --> 00:02:16,975
One.

54
00:02:16,509 --> 00:02:19,134
Diya's tank sits twelve
metres above the ground.

55
00:02:19,534 --> 00:02:20,434
Two.

56
00:02:20,036 --> 00:02:24,565
From the ground, one kilogram of its
water has a U of about one hundred

57
00:02:24,565 --> 00:02:25,973
and eighteen joules.

58
00:02:26,373 --> 00:02:27,273
Three.

59
00:02:26,935 --> 00:02:31,393
From the first floor, four metres up,
the same water has only seventy eight

60
00:02:31,393 --> 00:02:32,293
joules.

61
00:02:32,401 --> 00:02:33,301
Four.

62
00:02:32,978 --> 00:02:37,595
Water in the sump, two metres
below the ground, has a negative U.

63
00:02:37,595 --> 00:02:39,440
About minus twenty joules.

64
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,290
We choose the zero.

65
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:43,726
What matters is how much U changes.

66
00:02:44,326 --> 00:02:45,748
Now, side by side.

67
00:02:46,098 --> 00:02:47,916
Same two kilogram ball.

68
00:02:47,916 --> 00:02:50,887
Lift it twice as high, and U doubles.

69
00:02:51,287 --> 00:02:52,251
Same height.

70
00:02:52,251 --> 00:02:55,531
Use a ball twice as heavy,
and U doubles again.

71
00:02:56,131 --> 00:02:57,154
Now you try.

72
00:02:57,154 --> 00:03:01,730
A one kilogram ball on a four metre
shelf, or a two kilogram ball on a

73
00:03:01,730 --> 00:03:02,951
two metre shelf.

74
00:03:02,951 --> 00:03:04,430
Which stores more U?

75
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:05,700
Pause and decide.

76
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:09,800
Neither!

77
00:03:09,584 --> 00:03:11,480
m times h is four in both.

78
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,349
Each one stores thirty
nine point two joules.

79
00:03:14,999 --> 00:03:15,899
One more.

80
00:03:15,729 --> 00:03:19,244
A satellite is lifted two thousand
kilometres above the Earth.

81
00:03:19,244 --> 00:03:20,864
Can we still use m g h?

82
00:03:20,864 --> 00:03:21,958
Pause and think.

83
00:03:25,158 --> 00:03:26,058
No!

84
00:03:25,583 --> 00:03:28,392
Up there, g is only
about five point seven.

85
00:03:28,392 --> 00:03:31,922
m g h works only for heights
small next to Earth's radius.

86
00:03:32,572 --> 00:03:34,263
Now, one worked example.

87
00:03:34,613 --> 00:03:38,911
Diya's pump lifts five hundred litres
of water from the sump, two metres

88
00:03:38,911 --> 00:03:42,164
below the ground, to the
tank, twelve metres up.

89
00:03:42,164 --> 00:03:43,939
How much energy is stored?

90
00:03:44,439 --> 00:03:48,031
One litre of water has
a mass of one kilogram.

91
00:03:48,031 --> 00:03:50,495
So m is five hundred kilograms.

92
00:03:51,245 --> 00:03:54,100
The water climbs two
metres, then twelve more.

93
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,344
The height gained is fourteen metres.

94
00:03:57,094 --> 00:04:00,155
Change in U is m g
times the height gained.

95
00:04:00,155 --> 00:04:03,807
Five hundred, times nine
point eight, times fourteen.

96
00:04:04,557 --> 00:04:07,171
That is sixty eight
thousand six hundred joules.

97
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:09,409
The water carries it down to Diya's tap.

98
00:04:10,058 --> 00:04:11,520
Now, the exam trap.

99
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:15,138
A box is pushed five metres
up a ramp, at thirty degrees.

100
00:04:15,138 --> 00:04:17,198
Many students take h as five metres.

101
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:20,356
But h is the height climbed, straight up.

102
00:04:20,356 --> 00:04:23,467
Five times sine thirty
is two point five metres.

103
00:04:23,467 --> 00:04:25,018
Only the climb counts.

104
00:04:25,668 --> 00:04:27,054
Where is this asked?

105
00:04:27,054 --> 00:04:31,547
In short numericals on the change in
U, and inside bigger energy problems.

106
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:33,399
Exam level now.

107
00:04:33,399 --> 00:04:38,227
A five kilogram box goes from the
floor to a shelf two point five metres

108
00:04:38,227 --> 00:04:39,127
high.

109
00:04:38,821 --> 00:04:42,557
Take a one metre table
top as zero, and g as ten.

110
00:04:42,557 --> 00:04:45,358
Find U on the floor and on the shelf.

111
00:04:45,358 --> 00:04:46,663
Pause and solve.

112
00:04:52,063 --> 00:04:53,413
The answer is A.

113
00:04:53,413 --> 00:04:56,846
Minus fifty joules, and
plus seventy five joules.

114
00:04:57,346 --> 00:05:00,212
The floor is one metre below the zero.

115
00:05:00,212 --> 00:05:02,565
Five times ten times minus one.

116
00:05:02,565 --> 00:05:03,622
Minus fifty.

117
00:05:04,122 --> 00:05:07,555
The shelf is one point
five metres above the zero.

118
00:05:07,555 --> 00:05:10,087
Five times ten times one point five.

119
00:05:10,087 --> 00:05:11,450
Plus seventy five.

120
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:15,557
The change is still one
hundred and twenty five joules.

121
00:05:15,557 --> 00:05:17,049
Only the zero moved.

122
00:05:17,649 --> 00:05:19,189
Here is your recap.

123
00:05:19,189 --> 00:05:20,772
Screenshot this card.

124
00:05:23,972 --> 00:05:26,158
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

125
00:05:26,558 --> 00:05:27,458
One.

126
00:05:26,982 --> 00:05:30,069
Where does the water from a
rooftop tank get its energy?

127
00:05:30,969 --> 00:05:31,869
Two.

128
00:05:31,433 --> 00:05:33,674
How can potential energy be negative?

129
00:05:34,574 --> 00:05:35,474
Three.

130
00:05:35,124 --> 00:05:39,047
Why can we not use m g h for a
satellite, far above the Earth?

131
00:05:40,147 --> 00:05:43,973
Next time: a steep path and a
winding road up the same hill.

132
00:05:43,973 --> 00:05:46,307
Does gravity care which one you took?

133
00:05:46,307 --> 00:05:49,335
Find out in conservative
and non-conservative forces.
